id: pm-rz9gep
title: "MCP multi round-trip requests: input_required results, elicitation, retry state, and removal of server-initiated request assumptions"
description: Implement the 2026-07-28 MRTR pattern so pm can request bounded user or host input and continue the original operation through explicit inputResponses.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:mcp",elicitation,input-required,mrtr,retry,state-machine
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:08:41.357Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T17:57:14.660Z"
deadline: "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-25T17:55:30.479Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-25T17:55:30.479Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "All interim results use resultType input_required with typed bounded inputRequests and requestState; Retrying the original request with inputResponses resumes deterministically or returns an actionable expired or invalid-state refusal; No handler sends roots/list, sampling/createMessage, elicitation/create, or notifications/elicitation/complete as server-initiated RPC; Consent, secrets, authorization expansion, cancellation, duplicate retries, replay, and expiration have explicit negative tests; The SDK exposes a reusable MRTR state machine and MCP is a thin transport adapter"
goal: Explicit resumable interaction without reverse RPC
objective: Represent all server-needed input as typed inputRequests and resume through a retried original request
value: "Hosts can handle consent, clarification, and missing parameters without unsupported server-initiated calls or hidden sessions"
why_now: "2026-07-28 replaces roots/list, sampling/createMessage, elicitation/create, and similar reverse requests with MRTR"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented SDK-owned bounded multi-round-trip continuations with sealed request state, explicit input-required envelopes, deterministic retry, expiry, authorization binding, and replay protection."
expected_result: "Modern hosts can satisfy bounded input requests by retrying the original method with typed responses, without reverse RPC or hidden connection state."
actual_result: "The public interaction SDK and MCP adapter pass adversarial state, expiry, replay, malformed schema, synchronous, asynchronous, and real stateless protocol tests."
